Subject: [PATCH 31/67] test(aligram): claimJobsForFile atomicity scenarios
 11-13 + T-H9-3 doc reword (Phase 3.2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Scenarios 11-13 target the Phase 3.1 §11.6 open item: whether the
@Transaction on the claimJobsForFile default method actually wraps
the SELECT + N UPDATEs in one transaction.
- 11: 8 threads x 10 rounds claim the same file; each job must be
  claimed exactly once (busy/locked retries mirror scenario 4;
  production callers are single-threaded, so contention here is a
  harness artefact, not the property under test).
- 12: fault-injection trigger aborts the second COPYING update with
  NO outer transaction, so only the claim's own @Transaction can
  roll the first row back. Uses its own seed without a pre-existing
  COPYING row, otherwise the trigger would fire on the first update
  and the test would pass vacuously.
- 13: sequential double claim is a no-op (baseline for 11).
T-H9-3 comment reworded per the Phase 3.2 sent_messages re-check:
sent_messages is a Vector<int> of IDs, not a table; the premise
that a remote delete of an already-sent scheduled message travels
this update is unproven (Q1-Q3 need a device probe).
